<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1.0/policyconfig.dtd">
<!--
  Managed by macarchy.

  NOTE TO ANYONE EDITING THIS FILE: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML
  comment. Writing one here does not merely break the comment, it makes the
  whole document unparseable, polkitd registers none of the actions below, and
  pkexec silently falls back to its generic admin-auth action. The visible
  symptom is a password prompt that no rule can suppress, with nothing logged
  to explain it. Use an em dash instead.

  One action, not one per operation (randomize/restore/toggle/panic all share
  it) — following the same reasoning tormarchy uses for its own single
  "manage" action: they are all granted to the same user by the same rule, so
  separate actions would only be separate places to get this file wrong.

  Because the action pins a program path and not its arguments, granting it
  grants every subcommand. setup and uninstall refuse to run under pkexec at
  all (require_terminal_root) and require a real terminal with sudo, which
  keeps this grant scoped to the runtime commands.

  These defaults are the FALLBACK, not the normal path. 49-macarchy.rules
  grants this outright to the local, active user who ran setup, so that
  person is never prompted. Everyone else — another account on the box, or
  anyone arriving over SSH — lands here and has to authenticate.
-->
<policyconfig>
  <vendor>Macarchy</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/SalimRK/macarchy</vendor_url>

  <action id="com.macarchy.manage">
    <description>Manage network interface MAC addresses</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to change this machine's MAC address</message>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>auth_admin</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>auth_admin</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin_keep</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/local/bin/macarchy</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
